TianWen -- additional permission under GNU AGPL version 3 section 7
===================================================================

TianWen is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or (at
your option) any later version. The full text of that licence is in LICENSE. This
file states one additional permission, granted under section 7 of it.


Why this exists
---------------

TianWen drives astronomical hardware, and for most of that hardware the only way
to talk to it is a software development kit supplied by the manufacturer under its
own proprietary terms. Nobody but those vendors can relicense their SDKs under a
free licence. Without the permission below, conveying a working build of TianWen
would violate the licence, and the project could not ship the binaries it exists
to ship.

This is an ordinary and well-established use of section 7, not a loophole: the
permission loosens obligations only on my own code, and only far enough to let
TianWen talk to hardware.


The permission
--------------

As the sole copyright holder of TianWen, I give you permission to link or combine
TianWen with the proprietary software development kits, device drivers and runtime
libraries listed below, and to convey the resulting work. The terms of the GNU
Affero General Public License version 3 continue to apply to TianWen itself in
every other respect, including the obligation in section 13 to offer the
Corresponding Source to users interacting with a modified version over a network.

  * QHYCCD SDK (qhyccd.dll, libqhyccd.so, libqhyccd.dylib) -- QHYCCD
  * ZWO ASI SDK, including its camera, filter-wheel and focuser libraries -- ZWO
  * Canon EOS Digital SDK (EDSDK) and its RAW decoding components -- Canon Inc.
  * ASCOM Platform components, and any third-party ASCOM or Alpaca device driver
  * ONNX Runtime execution-provider libraries supplied by hardware vendors,
    including Qualcomm QNN and Microsoft DirectML
  * Any other software development kit, device driver or runtime library supplied
    by a hardware vendor that is required either to operate astronomical imaging,
    mount, focusing, filter or accessory hardware, or to run inference on that
    vendor's accelerator


What it does not do
-------------------

This permission covers combining TianWen with vendor software of the kind listed
above, and nothing more. In particular it does not permit conveying TianWen, or
any work based on it, under terms that withhold the corresponding source of
TianWen's own code, and it does not waive section 13. It grants nothing in respect
of the vendor software itself, which remains under its own terms, and nothing in
respect of anyone else's copyright.

As section 7 provides, you may remove this additional permission from any copy of
TianWen that you convey.
